talk(576,'1982-11-15','Yu. I. Manin','P001060-P001065','Twistor geometry and flag superspaces',r'The entry occupies P001061--P001063. After an agenda extending to supersymmetric field equations, Manin recalls the Grassmannian model of compactified complex Minkowski space, formulates a classification problem for flag superspaces, and explains the functor of points and two examples. The surviving text stops at the opening of the Penrose correspondence; it contains no worked new Yang--Mills solution. The closely related 1983 chapter is identifiable, but its full classification has not been verified here \citep{manin1983flags}.')
item(576,'P001061','method','The announced supertwistor programme',r'The agenda lists flag supermanifolds, a super Radon--Penrose transform, non-self-dual Yang--Mills solutions, deformations and supergravity, then the index and characteristic classes. Only the first four are promised.',r'This is a programme for encoding gauge fields by holomorphic data on superflag correspondences. No specific non-self-dual solution, deformation theorem, or index formula is stated in the surviving notes.','A',r'The programme has a close contemporary publication in \citet[abstract]{manin1983flags}; the ordinary holomorphic framework had already appeared in \citet{manin1981holomorphic}.',['manin1983flags','manin1981holomorphic'],match='partial',verification='publisher metadata checked',literal='not determinable',confidence='medium',status='the programme and its publication are identified; the notebook does not justify adding any absent solution or index theorem.')
item(576,'P001061-P001062','construction','Grassmannian compactification and null incidence',r'\(T=\mathbb C^4\), \(G(2,T)\) is compact complex Minkowski space; there are three-dimensional cones, two kinds of two-dimensional null planes, and null lines.',r'An affine chart of \(G(2,4)\) consists of graphs of \(2\times2\) matrices. The determinant gives the flat complex conformal quadratic form. At a point its rank-one tangent vectors form a three-dimensional null cone, ruled by the two families of totally null two-planes. A suitable real form and the affine chart recover real Minkowski space.','E',r'\citet[section~1, paragraph~2]{manin1981holomorphic} describes the graph construction before this talk.',['manin1981holomorphic'],reconstruction='The choice of real form, graph chart and determinant are supplied from the earlier source. The unexplained antiholomorphic involution on T plus T-dual is not promoted to a unique formula.')
item(576,'P001062','construction','Tautological bundles and spinors',r'The diagram places two rank-two bundles above \(G(2,T)\).',r'On \(G(2,T)\), the tautological bundle \(S\) and quotient bundle \(Q=T/S\) have rank two and \(TG(2,T)\simeq S^*\otimes Q\). On a chart and after the relevant real and determinant choices, these are the two spinor factors of the complexified tangent bundle.','E',r'This is the bundle geometry underlying \citet{manin1981holomorphic}.',['manin1981holomorphic'],reconstruction='The bundle identification is a standard reconstruction of the diagram; its handwritten bundle letters do not by themselves fix dual conventions.',match='partial')
mid=item(576,'P001062-P001063','problem','Flag superspaces with reduced space G(2,4)',r'\ru{Описать} homogeneous complex supermanifolds with reduced manifold \(G(2,T)\), requiring flags for simple Lie supergroups of classical type; only the beginning of a list follows.',r'Classify flag superspaces of classical simple complex Lie supergroups whose reduced complex manifold is isomorphic to \(G(2,4)\), specifying equivalence as homogeneous superspaces and the chosen class of flag stabilizers. The notebook supplies two families but does not claim its displayed list is complete.','A',r'\citet{manin1983flags} is the close contemporary account; later general flag structure appears in \citet[sections~5--6]{voronovmanin1990supercells}. The complete restricted list was not read in the 1983 source and is not certified by this annotation.',['manin1983flags','voronovmanin1990supercells'],reconstruction='Equivalence as homogeneous superspaces is made explicit; an underlying supermanifold classification could identify different homogeneous presentations.',match='partial',verification='publisher metadata checked',confidence='medium',problem='GP-1982-20',status='the classification programme has an identifiable 1983 publication; completeness of the precise restricted list remains unverified in this run, which is a verification limit, not an asserted open problem.')
P.append(dict(id='GP-1982-20',title='Flag superspaces with reduced Grassmannian G(2,4)',statement=r'Classify classical homogeneous flag superspaces whose reduced manifold is \(G(2,4)\), with equivalence and flag-stabilizer convention specified.',occurrences=[mid],status=r'As of November 2026: Manin’s 1983 chapter is the close publication match. Its complete classification has not been independently read; this entry does not assert that the question is still open.',status_date='2026-11',refs=['manin1983flags','voronovmanin1990supercells']))
item(576,'P001062','definition','Superflags require the functor of points',r'A naive flag of complex supervector spaces has too few coordinates; for every supercommutative algebra \(A\), use projective direct submodules and base change \(A\to B\).',r'The functor \(A\mapsto\{N^{2|0}\subset N^{2|N}\subset A^{4|N}\}\), with locally free quotients and locally direct summands, is represented by the flag superscheme. Scalar extension defines its covariant action on superalgebras. Restriction to ordinary complex points discards all odd directions.','E',r'The standard representable-functor definition is used in \citet[sections~1--2]{voronovmanin1990supercells}; it is background, rather than a new 1988 discovery.',['voronovmanin1990supercells'],reconstruction='Locally free quotient conditions clarify the notebook’s projective direct-submodule shorthand.')
item(576,'P001062','construction','The standard N-extended superspace flag',r'\(F(2|0,2|N;\mathbb C^{4|N})\) has dimension \(4|4N\); its real big cell is the physicists\textquotesingle\ \(N\)-extended superspace.',r'The indicated flag superspace has reduced manifold \(G(2,4)\), even dimension \(4\) and odd dimension \(4N\). Its big cell admits four even coordinates and two sets of \(2N\) odd spinor coordinates. A real superspace requires an appropriate real structure; its compact flag ambient space supplies the stated conformal completion.','A',r'This is the concrete superflag setting of \citet{manin1983flags}; the flag formalism is checked against \citet[section~1]{voronovmanin1990supercells}.',['manin1983flags','voronovmanin1990supercells'],match='partial',reconstruction='The real structure is an extra choice, not specified by the complex flag alone.',verification='publisher metadata checked',confidence='medium')
item(576,'P001062','construction','Projective supercoordinates and their big cells',r'\(G(1|0,\mathbb C^{m|n})=\mathbb P^{m-1|n}\), with ratios by \(x_i\); the last odd ratio is written \(\xi_m/x_i\).',r'On the chart \(x_i\ne0\), the independent coordinates are \(x_j/x_i\) for \(j\ne i\) and \(\xi_a/x_i\) for \(1\le a\le n\). Thus each chart has dimension \((m-1)|n\), and these charts are the simplest superflag big cells.','E',r'The projective-bundle construction is part of the established superflag formalism \citep[section~1]{voronovmanin1990supercells}.',['voronovmanin1990supercells'],literal='false as written',reconstruction='The omitted even coordinate equals 1; the last odd index is corrected from m to n.')
item(576,'P001062','question','Classes of odd-codimension supercells',r'An equation \(\xi_i=0\) gives codimension \(0|1\). The notes ask what cohomology contains such cells; ordinary differential and integral forms serve only extreme dimensions, while Schwarz’s intermediate objects have strange properties.',r'The local subsupermanifold cut out by one independent odd coordinate has codimension \(0|1\). The question seeks a cohomology or intersection theory representing such supercycles, but does not specify admissible cycles, equivalence, degree conventions, or required operations.','F',r'\citet[introduction]{voronovmanin1990supercells} still explains the need for a suitable theory in 1988 and names candidate constructions. That historical discussion does not establish either a universal solution or present-day openness of every formulation.',['voronovmanin1990supercells'],literal='not determinable',match='thematic only',verification='read the result',confidence='medium',status='the requested theory is insufficiently specified to attach a single resolved/open label.')
item(576,'P001062-P001063','construction','The odd-form isotropic example',r'The second entry is \(FI(2|0,2|2;\mathbb C^{4|4},\Pi\mathrm{Sp})\), dimension \(4|8\), with an odd symmetric form; further series and isolated examples are merely mentioned.',r'The notebook specifies an isotropic flag superspace for a nondegenerate odd symmetric form, with the displayed dimension. A complete interpretation must fix the periplectic form and isotropy conventions; the unnamed further examples cannot be reconstructed as an exhaustive list.','A',r'The example belongs to the programme of \citet{manin1983flags}. The distinction between classical types and their isotropic flag conventions is developed in \citet[sections~2,5]{voronovmanin1990supercells}.',['manin1983flags','voronovmanin1990supercells'],match='partial',verification='publisher metadata checked',confidence='medium',reconstruction='The modern term periplectic is supplied for the odd symmetric form; no absent series is inserted.')
item(576,'P001063','method','The Penrose correspondence starts but is not recorded',r'The last two symbols are \(M=G(2,T)\), \(P(T)=G(1,T)\).',r'These are the space-time and projective twistor spaces. Their usual incidence space is \(F(1,2;T)\), with projections to both Grassmannians; this incidence space is editorial reconstruction. No transform, cohomology degree, or field equation is stated on the surviving final page.','E',r'The ordinary correspondence predates the talk \citep{manin1981holomorphic}; the fragment does not license importing the unrecorded supertransform.',['manin1981holomorphic'],reconstruction='The incidence space identifies the geometric context but is not drawn or defined in the final fragment.',match='partial')
correction('P001062','Projective superspace chart',r'Last odd coordinate \(\xi_m/x_i\).',r'\(\xi_n/x_i\); omit \(x_i/x_i=1\) from independent even coordinates.',r'Scan and Russian agree on m, while the preceding homogeneous list has n odd variables. The dimension and coordinate list force the correction.')
save()
