talk(578,'1982-11-29','I. Yu. Kobzarev','P001069-P001073','Domain walls, vortex strings and the Nambu action',r'The actual talk is P001070--P001073. A scalar double well supplies a planar wall; the Abelian Higgs model supplies a vortex string. Integrating a thin core yields the Nambu worldsheet action, with a collapsing circular loop as an illustration. The final page introduces the colour gauge Lagrangian. These are expository constructions predating the talk; the wall formula can be checked against Kobzarev’s own 1974 paper. The notes suppress couplings and contain a gauge-sign mismatch.')
item(578,'P001070','definition','Scalar field equations and polynomial interactions',r'\(\Box\psi+\mu^2\psi=0\), with interactions such as \(\lambda\varphi_1\varphi_2\varphi_3\).',r'A real scalar field on Minkowski space with quadratic kinetic and mass terms obeys the Klein--Gordon equation; polynomial potential terms change the Euler--Lagrange equation by the corresponding derivative. The date 1970 is a rhetorical contrast with soliton methods, not the historical invention of nonlinear field theory.','E',r'The interacting scalar setting is already explicit in \citet[section~2]{zeldovichkobzarevokun1975walls}.',['zeldovichkobzarevokun1975walls'],literal='correct',match='partial')
item(578,'P001070','construction','A double-well potential and two classical vacua',r'\(\mathcal L=\tfrac12(\partial\varphi)^2-\lambda^2(\varphi^2-\eta^2)^2\); the Hamiltonian is nonnegative, with vacua \(\varphi=\pm\eta\) exchanged by a discrete symmetry.',r'For positive \(\lambda,\eta\), with Minkowski kinetic convention, the static energy density is \(\tfrac12|\nabla\varphi|^2+\lambda^2(\varphi^2-\eta^2)^2\). Its homogeneous minima are exactly \(\pm\eta\); choosing one breaks the global \(\mathbb Z/2\) symmetry of the classical Lagrangian.','E',r'\citet[section~2]{zeldovichkobzarevokun1975walls} gives the same scalar potential before the lecture.',['zeldovichkobzarevokun1975walls'],literal='correct with missing hypotheses')
item(578,'P001070-P001071','construction','The planar domain wall and its thickness',r'The field tends to \(\pm\eta\) as \(z\to\pm\infty\); the equation lacks a factor 4 and the solution is written \(\tanh(z\eta)\).',r'For the preceding normalization the field equation is \(\Box\varphi+4\lambda^2\varphi(\varphi^2-\eta^2)=0\). A static planar wall independent of t,x,y is \(\varphi(z)=\eta\tanh(\sqrt2\lambda\eta(z-z_0))\). Its characteristic width is of order \((\lambda\eta)^{-1}\); its energy is finite per unit area, not finite over the whole infinite plane.','E',r'The correctly normalized profile and width are already in \citet[section~3]{zeldovichkobzarevokun1975walls}.',['zeldovichkobzarevokun1975walls'],literal='false as written',reconstruction='The translation parameter and the distinction between total and per-area energy are explicit. Substitution and a first-integral check are recorded independently in checks.py.')
item(578,'P001071','definition','Local U(1) covariance of the Abelian Higgs action',r'The covariant derivative is \(\partial+iA\), but the printed transformation has \(\varphi\mapsto e^{i\alpha}\varphi\), \(A\mapsto A+d\alpha\).',r'With \(D=d+iA\), covariance requires \(A\mapsto A-d\alpha\). Then \(D\varphi\) transforms by the same phase as \(\varphi\), and the Maxwell term, scalar kinetic term and potential \((|\varphi|^2-\eta^2)^2\) are gauge invariant. A coupling can be restored consistently as \(D=d+ieA\).','E',r'The Abelian Higgs starting point is \citet[section~2, equation~2.1]{nielsenolesen1973vortex}.',['nielsenolesen1973vortex'],literal='false as written')
item(578,'P001071-P001072','construction','Vortex winding and flux quantization',r'A transverse circuit rotates the vacuum vector once; \(\varphi_1=(x/r)f(r)\), \(\varphi_2=(y/r)f(r)\), approaching the vacuum at infinity.',r'A smooth static straight vortex of winding n has \(\varphi\sim\eta e^{in\theta}\) at large radius, vanishing core amplitude, and a gauge field with \(D\varphi\to0\). For \(D=d+ieA\), finite energy per unit length gives \(\int F=-2\pi n/e\) in this orientation. The profiles satisfy coupled nonlinear radial equations; the displayed ansatz is not an elementary closed-form solution.','E',r'\citet[section~2, equations~2.4--2.13]{nielsenolesen1973vortex} derives the flux and radial ansatz in 1973.',['nielsenolesen1973vortex'],reconstruction='General winding, finite-energy boundary conditions and the gauge-field role complete the one-winding diagram.')
item(578,'P001072','method','The thin-core approximation produces a string action',r'If the curvature radius greatly exceeds the thickness, \(S\simeq\nu\int dl\sqrt{1-v_\perp^2}\,dt\), where \(\nu\) is energy per length.',r'For a slowly varying vortex with core width much smaller than all relevant curvature radii, with internal excitations neglected, integrating the transverse profile gives the leading Nambu--Goto action \(S_{eff}=-\nu\int\sqrt{-\det h}\,d^2\sigma\), up to the overall action-sign convention. The approximation ceases to control regions with curvature on the core scale.','E',r'The same reduction and transverse-velocity argument are \citet[section~3, equations~3.3--3.6]{nielsenolesen1973vortex}.',['nielsenolesen1973vortex'],reconstruction='The hypotheses are a physical effective-description regime, not an error estimate proved in the notebook.')
item(578,'P001072-P001073','definition','Worldsheet area and extremality',r'The moving string sweeps a sheet; its area is called the Lagrangian, followed by minimum area.',r'The induced worldsheet metric is \(h_{ab}=\eta_{\mu\nu}\partial_aX^\mu\partial_bX^\nu\). The Nambu--Goto action is proportional to its Lorentzian area. Its Euler--Lagrange equations express stationarity, equivalently vanishing mean-curvature vector for a smooth timelike immersion, with suitable boundary conditions. They do not assert a Euclidean minimum.','E',r'The area and variation formulas are displayed in \citet[sections~1.2--1.2.2]{tong2009string}, as an exposition of the older construction.',['tong2009string'],literal='false as written',reconstruction='Action versus Lagrangian density and Lorentzian stationarity are distinguished.')
item(578,'P001072','claim','A circular loop contracts in the effective model',r'A ring-shaped string contracts, quickly reaches the speed of light and becomes a small lump.',r'For an initially resting circular Nambu--Goto loop in flat space, \(R(t)=R_0\cos(t/R_0)\) until the first collapse, \(0\le t<\pi R_0/2\). Its inward speed tends to 1 at collapse. For a field-theory vortex, the thin-core approximation fails before zero radius, so this does not determine the final lump or radiation.','E',r'This follows from the classical action explained in \citet[section~1.2]{tong2009string}; the finite-core limitation is already part of \citet[section~3]{nielsenolesen1973vortex}.',['tong2009string','nielsenolesen1973vortex'],reconstruction='The exact circular solution makes the qualitative claim precise only within the effective model; its conserved-energy and equation-of-motion checks are recorded in checks.py.')
item(578,'P001072','remark','Monopoles as string endpoints',r'A variant places a monopole at each broken end of a string.',r'The diagram proposes a flux tube ending on magnetic sources. The smooth pure Abelian Higgs model on all of Minkowski space does not itself supply nonsingular monopole cores: one must add magnetic defects, boundary conditions, or an enlarged gauge theory. None of these is specified.','F',r'An identifiable earlier lead is \citet{kobayashi1974monopoles}, whose title and metadata match the idea. Its particular model cannot be assigned to this unspecified sketch.',['kobayashi1974monopoles'],literal='not determinable',match='thematic only',verification='publisher metadata checked',confidence='medium',status='the source does not fix an endpoint model; this is not catalogued as an unsolved monopole-existence problem.')
item(578,'P001073','definition','The colour gauge field and quark Lagrangian',r'\(SU(3)\) acts in the adjoint on the eight gauge components and in the triplet on quarks; two terms for u and d are displayed.',r'For a chosen convention, \(\mathcal L=-\tfrac14F^a_{\mu\nu}F^{a\mu\nu}+\sum_f\bar q_f(i\gamma^\mu D_\mu-m_f)q_f\), with \(D_\mu=\partial_\mu-igA_\mu^at^a\), \([t^a,t^b]=if^{abc}t^c\), and \(F^a_{\mu\nu}=\partial_\mu A^a_\nu-\partial_\nu A^a_\mu+gf^{abc}A^b_\mu A^c_\nu\). The adjoint dimension is 8 and the fundamental dimension 3. A two-flavour truncation is a model, not a claim that there are only two flavours.','E',r'The colour gauge-theory framework predates the talk \citep{grosswilczek1973ultraviolet}. The present note records a definition; no confinement theorem is stated.',['grosswilczek1973ultraviolet'],verification='publisher metadata checked',reconstruction='A consistent sign and coupling convention replaces the notebook’s mixed D and F formulas, and separate flavour masses are restored.',match='partial')
correction('P001070','Equation 6',r'\(\Box\varphi+\lambda^2\varphi(\varphi^2-\eta^2)=0\).',r'Insert 4 before \(\lambda^2\).',r'Scan confirms no 4. Differentiate the preceding potential; independent confirmation is the 1974 Kobzarev coauthored wall paper, section~3.')
correction('P001070','After equation~7','Independent of x,y,z.','Independent of t,x,y for the displayed z-dependent static wall.',r'The source list includes z, contradicting the asymptotic condition immediately before it; the intended planar wall fixes the emendation.')
correction('P001071','Wall profile and thickness',r'\(\tanh(z\eta)\), width of order \(1/\eta\).',r'For equation~2 use \(\eta\tanh(\sqrt2\lambda\eta z)\), width of order \((\lambda\eta)^{-1}\).',r'The amplitude and coupling are absent in the scan. The printed potential and boundary values determine them; a rescaling would have to be stated.')
correction('P001071','Equations 9, 12, 13','D=d+iA and A maps to A+dalpha for phase exp(ialpha).','With that phase and D, use A maps to A-dalpha.',r'All three plus signs are visible in the scan. Direct differentiation produces an extra \(2i\,d\alpha\) unless one sign is changed.')
correction('P001073','Top line','Minimum area.','Stationary Lorentzian worldsheet area.',r'The scan says min. The timelike Nambu action has an indefinite second variation; its equation is an extremality condition.')
correction('P001073','Equations 23, 24, 26','D has no coupling factor while F has g; sign conventions are not specified.','Choose one consistent generator, D and F convention.',r'Scan confirms the unequal appearances of g. Either absorb it throughout or retain it in both the covariant derivative and curvature.',typ='ambiguity')
save()
